id: pm-vcs-sl77
title: Honor disabled HTTP Date headers when serving with native Bun
description: "Separate native Bun compatibility finding from PR #91 path catalogue validation. Bun 1.3.5 emits an automatic Date header despite response.sendDate=false in engine/serve.ts; Node omits it. Two identical denial responses across a one-second refresh wait therefore differ only in Date. Status and denial body are identical, and no repository existence disclosure was observed. Investigate a portable omission or a bounded stable header policy and add a cross-second raw socket regression without altering the path catalogue."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T09:04:49.913Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T22:18:15.800Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-sol
parent: pm-vcs-5h6j
repro_steps: "Run a native Bun server with response.sendDate=false; send the same denied POST twice more than one second apart; compare raw response headers. engine/serve.ts follows this pattern, and the new directory-replacement socket fixture reproduced differing Date values."
expected_result: The requested suppression of automatic Date headers is honored under both supported runtimes.
actual_result: Node omits Date; native Bun 1.3.5 emits a changing Date header.
